IMPORT prelude

-- Miscellaneous Offences (Public Order and Nuisance) Act 1906 (Singapore) -- the offences an ordinary person or business meets:
-- dog owners' liability (s 10), spitting (s 11(1)(f), (2)), emergency-line calls and the subscriber's liability (ss 14A, 14B), false
-- messages (s 14D), soliciting and disorderly behaviour (ss 19, 20), trespass (s 21), touting (ss 32, 33), fraudulent possession and
-- the secondhand dealer's duty (ss 35, 36), melting precious metals within 5 days (ss 37, 39), and lending out a SIM card (s 39B).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/MOPONA1906.txt. The revised
-- edition itself "incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021"; later amendments are annotated in the text, the
-- latest being Act 21 of 2025 (wef 17/08/2026, the new ss 14E, 37 and 39; and wef 30/12/2025, the SIM card penalties).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 5 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository. SCOPED to offences with decision content:
-- elements, exceptions, presumptions and the maximum (and in s 32 minimum) penalties. Not encoded: ss 6-9, 12, 13, 15-17, 22-31,
-- 34, 14C, 14E, 39C-39I, police powers (ss 7, 14(2), 40), corporate and partnership liability (ss 40A, 40B), and the Schedule of
-- scam offences. Arrestability and court jurisdiction (s 4) are not modelled.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Miscellaneous Offences (Public Order and Nuisance) Act 1906 -- offences`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lesser of` MEANS
    IF `a` AT MOST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

§§ `10 -- liability of dog owner`

-- s 10(1): "Any owner of a dog which causes injury to any person" -- fine not exceeding $5,000. (2) "In addition to any fine",
-- compensation "not exceeding $2,000 is payable to the person injured". (4) no need to show "a previous vicious propensity" or the
-- owner's knowledge or neglect. (7), (8): no compensation and no criminal liability for an injury inside a house or premises unless
-- the person entered "in the ordinary course of the person's duties or with the express or implied permission of the occupier".
-- (9): "The owner shall not be liable under this section for any injury ... attributable to any wrongful act of that person."
GIVEN `the dog injured the person` IS A BOOLEAN, `the injury was inside premises` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the person entered on duty or with permission` IS A BOOLEAN, `the injury was due to the person's own wrongful act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the dog owner is liable under section 10` IF
        `the dog injured the person`
    AND ((NOT `the injury was inside premises`) OR `the person entered on duty or with permission`)
    AND (NOT `the injury was due to the person's own wrongful act`)

GIVEN `the dog injured the person` IS A BOOLEAN, `the injury was inside premises` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the person entered on duty or with permission` IS A BOOLEAN, `the injury was due to the person's own wrongful act` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the damage assessed by the court` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the section 10 compensation` MEANS
    IF `the dog owner is liable under section 10` `the dog injured the person` `the injury was inside premises` `the person entered on duty or with permission` `the injury was due to the person's own wrongful act`
    THEN `the lesser of` `the damage assessed by the court` 2000
    ELSE 0

-- s 10(5): the occupier of premises where the dog was kept "is deemed to be the owner of the dog ... unless the occupier can prove"
-- BOTH (a) he or she was not the owner and (b) the dog was kept there "without his or her sanction or knowledge".
GIVEN `the dog was kept at the occupier's premises` IS A BOOLEAN, `the occupier proved not the owner` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the occupier proved no sanction or knowledge` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the occupier is deemed the dog's owner` IF
    `the dog was kept at the occupier's premises` AND (NOT (`the occupier proved not the owner` AND `the occupier proved no sanction or knowledge`))

§§ `11(1)(f), (2) -- spitting`

-- s 11(1)(f): spitting in a coffee shop, market, public conveyance, public road, five-foot way "or in any other place to which the
-- public has or may have access" -- fine not exceeding $1,000; (2) after a previous conviction under (1)(f), not exceeding $2,000.
GIVEN `previously convicted of spitting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine for spitting` MEANS
    IF `previously convicted of spitting` THEN 2000 ELSE 1000

§§ `14A, 14B -- calls to emergency telephone numbers`

-- s 14A(1): a call "with intent to annoy, abuse, threaten or harass" the person answering -- $5,000 or one year or both.
-- (2): an obscene, lewd, lascivious, filthy or indecent communication -- $10,000 or 3 years or both.
-- (3): from a PUBLIC telephone -- (a) $10,000 or 2 years; (b) $20,000 or 5 years.
DECLARE EmergencyCall IS ONE OF
    `a harassing call`
    `an obscene call`

GIVEN `the call` IS AN EmergencyCall, `from a public telephone` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine for the call` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the call`
    WHEN `a harassing call` THEN (IF `from a public telephone` THEN 10000 ELSE 5000)
    WHEN `an obscene call` THEN (IF `from a public telephone` THEN 20000 ELSE 10000)

GIVEN `the call` IS AN EmergencyCall, `from a public telephone` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum years for the call` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the call`
    WHEN `a harassing call` THEN (IF `from a public telephone` THEN 2 ELSE 1)
    WHEN `an obscene call` THEN (IF `from a public telephone` THEN 5 ELSE 3)

-- s 14A(4)(b): a caller who "refuses to speak or immediately hangs up is presumed until the contrary is proved to have intent to
-- annoy".
GIVEN `the caller stayed silent or hung up` IS A BOOLEAN, `the caller proved otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `intent to annoy is presumed` IF
    `the caller stayed silent or hung up` AND (NOT `the caller proved otherwise`)

-- s 14B(1): the subscriber to a telephone service used for a s 14A offence is guilty "unless the person proves ... that the person
-- had exercised due diligence" -- $5,000. (2) not the subscriber of a public telephone service.
GIVEN `the line was used for a 14A offence` IS A BOOLEAN, `it is a public telephone service` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the subscriber proved due diligence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the subscriber is guilty` IF
        `the line was used for a 14A offence`
    AND (NOT `it is a public telephone service`)
    AND (NOT `the subscriber proved due diligence`)

§§ `14D -- communicating a false message`

-- s 14D(1): transmitting "a message which the person knows to be false or fabricated" -- $10,000 or 3 years or both. (1A) (Act 16
-- of 2024): not guilty if the person proves, on a balance of probabilities, "a legitimate purpose related to public order, public
-- safety or national security, or the prevention, investigation or prosecution of offences" -- illustrated by a government
-- simulated-phishing email.
GIVEN `transmitted the message` IS A BOOLEAN, `knew it was false` IS A BOOLEAN, `proved a legitimate purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the false message is an offence` IF
    `transmitted the message` AND `knew it was false` AND (NOT `proved a legitimate purpose`)

§§ `19, 20 -- soliciting and disorderly behaviour`

-- s 19: persistently loitering or soliciting for prostitution "or for any other immoral purpose" -- $1,000; second or subsequent
-- conviction -- $2,000 or 6 months or both. (A first conviction carries no imprisonment.)
-- s 20: riotous, disorderly or indecent behaviour in a public road, public place, or near a court, police station or place of worship
-- -- $2,000 or 6 months or both; second or subsequent -- $5,000 or 12 months or both.
DECLARE PublicOrderOffence IS ONE OF
    `soliciting in a public place`
    `disorderly behaviour`

GIVEN `the offence` IS A PublicOrderOffence, `a second or subsequent conviction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine for the public order offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `soliciting in a public place` THEN (IF `a second or subsequent conviction` THEN 2000 ELSE 1000)
    WHEN `disorderly behaviour` THEN (IF `a second or subsequent conviction` THEN 5000 ELSE 2000)

GIVEN `the offence` IS A PublicOrderOffence, `a second or subsequent conviction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum months for the public order offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `soliciting in a public place` THEN (IF `a second or subsequent conviction` THEN 6 ELSE 0)
    WHEN `disorderly behaviour` THEN (IF `a second or subsequent conviction` THEN 12 ELSE 6)

§§ `21 -- wilful trespass`

-- s 21(1): wilfully trespassing "without satisfactory excuse" on Government ground, a dwelling house or premises, or a boat or vessel,
-- "not thereby ... causing any actual damage, or not causing in the opinion of the Magistrate's Court more than nominal damage" --
-- $1,000. (A trespass causing more than nominal damage falls outside s 21; the Act does not say where it goes instead.)
GIVEN `wilfully trespassed` IS A BOOLEAN, `had a satisfactory excuse` IS A BOOLEAN, `caused more than nominal damage` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the trespass is a section 21 offence` IF
    `wilfully trespassed` AND (NOT `had a satisfactory excuse`) AND (NOT `caused more than nominal damage`)

§§ `32, 33 -- touting`

-- s 32: touting persistently or annoyingly in a public road, public place or vehicle, in connection with any trade or business --
-- "a fine of not less than $1,000 and not more than $5,000" or 6 months or both; second or subsequent -- "not less than $2,000 and
-- not more than $10,000" or one year or both. One of the few MINIMUM fines in the Act.
GIVEN `a second or subsequent conviction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the minimum touting fine` MEANS
    IF `a second or subsequent conviction` THEN 2000 ELSE 1000

GIVEN `a second or subsequent conviction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum touting fine` MEANS
    IF `a second or subsequent conviction` THEN 10000 ELSE 5000

GIVEN `a second or subsequent conviction` IS A BOOLEAN, `the fine` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the touting fine is within the statutory range` IF
    `the fine` AT LEAST `the minimum touting fine` `a second or subsequent conviction`
    AND `the fine` AT MOST `the maximum touting fine` `a second or subsequent conviction`

-- s 33(1): touting services at or near a "public office" (any court and Government office or department) -- $2,000 or 6 months.
-- (2): does not apply to (a) an officer appointed to advise the public on that office's business, (b) a licensed or authorised
-- petition writer.
DECLARE Tout IS ONE OF
    `an unlicensed agent`
    `an officer appointed to advise the public`
    `a licensed petition writer`

GIVEN `the tout` IS A Tout
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 33 applies to the tout` IF
    CONSIDER `the tout`
    WHEN `an unlicensed agent` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `35, 36 -- fraudulent possession; the secondhand dealer's duty`

-- s 35(1): possessing or conveying anything "reasonably suspected of being stolen or fraudulently obtained" and failing "to account
-- satisfactorily" -- $3,000 or one year or both. (5): after a previous conviction under s 35 or Chapter 12 or 17 of the Penal Code --
-- or a similar conviction "in Malaysia or in Brunei Darussalam" -- $5,000 or 2 years or both.
GIVEN `possesses suspected stolen property` IS A BOOLEAN, `accounted satisfactorily` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the possession is a section 35 offence` IF
    `possesses suspected stolen property` AND (NOT `accounted satisfactorily`)

GIVEN `has a qualifying previous conviction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine for fraudulent possession` MEANS
    IF `has a qualifying previous conviction` THEN 5000 ELSE 3000

GIVEN `has a qualifying previous conviction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum years for fraudulent possession` MEANS
    IF `has a qualifying previous conviction` THEN 2 ELSE 1

-- s 36(1), (2): a secondhand dealer or money changer given a police description, holding or offered matching property, must inform
-- the police "without undue delay" -- $1,000. (3): where the property is "difficult to identify no fine is to be imposed ... unless
-- the court is of the opinion that the property has been wilfully concealed".
GIVEN `got a police description` IS A BOOLEAN, `held or was offered matching property` IS A BOOLEAN, `informed the police` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the property is difficult to identify` IS A BOOLEAN, `the dealer wilfully concealed it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the dealer may be fined under section 36` IF
        `got a police description` AND `held or was offered matching property` AND (NOT `informed the police`)
    AND ((NOT `the property is difficult to identify`) OR `the dealer wilfully concealed it`)

§§ `37, 39 -- melting or defacing metals within 5 days of receipt`

-- s 37(3): "relevant person" -- (a) a pawnbroker or dealer in secondhand goods; (b) a worker in platinum, gold or silver; (c) a
-- dealer in platinum, gold or silver articles. s 39: nothing in s 37 applies to a person EMPLOYED by such a worker or dealer for the
-- business.
-- s 37(1): a relevant person who melts, alters, defaces, disposes of or sells goods, metals or articles is guilty if (c) it was done
-- (i) "within 5 days of receipt ... from any person other than another relevant person" or (ii) after police information that they
-- were stolen; (d) without the previous permission of the Director, Criminal Investigation Department; AND (e) "the goods, metals or
-- articles were in fact stolen or fraudulently obtained". (2): $5,000 or 6 months or both. (Act 21 of 2025, wef 17/08/2026.)
-- "Within 5 days" is read here as 5 days or fewer (an inference; the cases avoid the boundary).
DECLARE Handler IS ONE OF
    `a pawnbroker`
    `a dealer in secondhand goods`
    `a goldsmith`
    `a dealer in gold articles`
    `a goldsmith's employee`
    `a member of the public`

GIVEN `the handler` IS A Handler
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the handler is a relevant person` IF
    CONSIDER `the handler`
    WHEN `a goldsmith's employee` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a member of the public` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the handler` IS A Handler, `days since receipt` IS A NUMBER, `received from another relevant person` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `told by police it was stolen` IS A BOOLEAN, `had CID permission` IS A BOOLEAN, `it was in fact stolen` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `melting or selling it is a section 37 offence` IF
        `the handler is a relevant person` `the handler`
    AND (    (`days since receipt` AT MOST 5 AND (NOT `received from another relevant person`))
         OR  `told by police it was stolen`)
    AND (NOT `had CID permission`)
    AND `it was in fact stolen`

§§ `39B -- providing a SIM card registered in one's own name`

-- s 39B(1): providing, or offering, "a SIM card registered using the person's personal information to another person", knowing or
-- having reasonable grounds to believe it is for (b)(i) committing or facilitating any offence, or (b)(ii) wrongful gain or loss.
-- (2): for limb (b)(i), reasonable grounds are presumed until the contrary is proved if (a) the act is done "for any gain", or (b)
-- the person "fails to take reasonable steps to ascertain" the recipient's identity and physical location, or the purpose.
GIVEN `did it for any gain` IS A BOOLEAN, `took reasonable steps to ascertain identity and location` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `took reasonable steps to ascertain purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reasonable grounds to believe are presumed` IF
        `did it for any gain`
    OR  (NOT `took reasonable steps to ascertain identity and location`)
    OR  (NOT `took reasonable steps to ascertain purpose`)

-- s 39B(4): (a) an individual -- $10,000 or 3 years or both; (b) any other case -- $20,000 (a fine only).
GIVEN `the offender is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine for providing the SIM card` MEANS
    IF `the offender is an individual` THEN 10000 ELSE 20000

GIVEN `the offender is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum years for providing the SIM card` MEANS
    IF `the offender is an individual` THEN 3 ELSE 0

-- s 39B(5) (Act 21 of 2025, wef 30/12/2025): an individual convicted under limb (b)(i) is ALSO liable to "caning of not more than
-- 12 strokes" (a) if he or she knew the SIM card was for a scam offence, or (b) if it is proved the card was used for a scam offence
-- and the individual "is not able to prove" having taken reasonable steps to ensure it would not be.
GIVEN `the offender is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN, `convicted on the offence limb` IS A BOOLEAN, `knew it was for a scam` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the card was proved used for a scam` IS A BOOLEAN, `proved reasonable steps against scam use` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `caning is available` IF
        `the offender is an individual`
    AND `convicted on the offence limb`
    AND (`knew it was for a scam` OR (`the card was proved used for a scam` AND (NOT `proved reasonable steps against scam use`)))

GIVEN `the offender is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN, `convicted on the offence limb` IS A BOOLEAN, `knew it was for a scam` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the card was proved used for a scam` IS A BOOLEAN, `proved reasonable steps against scam use` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum strokes` MEANS
    IF `caning is available` `the offender is an individual` `convicted on the offence limb` `knew it was for a scam` `the card was proved used for a scam` `proved reasonable steps against scam use`
    THEN 12
    ELSE 0
